This boring work is finally finished.
I am very relieved.
I make a cup of chai for myself.
I take my phone and go to the balcony.
It is raining lightly outside.
I make a video call to my younger sister, Sofia, in Mexico.
Sofia answers the phone immediately.
"Hello Maya, how are you?" she asks.
"I am fine, I have just filled out a very boring online form," I say.
Sofia starts laughing loudly.
"We both often put off such tasks," she says.
"Yes, usually I put off these tasks for weeks," I admit.
We both laugh at this habit of ours.
"But it always feels very good after the work is finished," Sofia says.
"Exactly, usually work is done very slowly on these websites," I say.
This is a very small victory, but we are both feeling happy.
I stand in the balcony and comfortably drink my chai.
Talking to Sofia always makes my day better.
